2026-11-18 The Open Kannada Authors (1.300)
	* Ready for release. PostScript name Gari-Regular and full name Gari
	Regular, no embedding restriction (fsType 0), vendor ID NONE, and a
	copyright line without line breaks. Typo, hhea and Windows metrics
	now agree: ascent 2160 and descent 1464 with no line gap, which keeps
	the previous line height on macOS. tools/finish.py drops FontForge's
	FFTM table and the Macintosh name records, maps U+00A0 to the space,
	and writes unique glyph names. The license record holds the short OFL
	statement (the full text ships as OFL.txt), and the Navilu Reserved
	Font Name notice follows Aravinda VK's copyright line.
	* U+200C ZERO WIDTH NON-JOINER and U+200D ZERO WIDTH JOINER map to
	empty glyphs with no width.
	* tools/release.py builds TTF, OTF, WOFF2, a Kannada web subset, a
	specimen and checksums. FONTLOG.txt added.
	* Renamed COPYING to OFL.txt. Removed tools/generate_fonts.py, an
	unused GPL script from upstream, and upstream's FUNDING.yml. Added
	NOTICE.md and CONTRIBUTING.md. Scripts and tests written for this
	fork are under MIT OR Apache-2.0.
	* Renamed to Gari. Navilu is a Reserved Font Name under its SIL Open
	Font License, so a modified version cannot use it.
	* Added new-order Kannada shaping (knd2). Every lookup registered for
	knda is also registered for knd2. The below-base ligatures get knd2
	twins with virama first. For a cluster that ends in a virama, a knd2
	contextual rule gives the base its virama form and a pair adjustment
	draws the virama on the base, as old-order shaping does.
	tools/add_knd2.py makes these changes.
	* Added shaping tests (tests/test_shaping.py) and CI.
	* Added U+0CDC KANNADA ARCHAIC SHRII, U+0CDD KANNADA LETTER
	NAKAARA POLLU and U+0CF3 KANNADA SIGN COMBINING ANUSVARA ABOVE RIGHT,
	drafted with kannadi tools/glyphdraft from Gari's own stems, weight and
	anusvara. Drafts for a Kannada reader to approve.

